  "summary": "Nepali architecture or Nepalese architecture is influenced by the architecture of India, Tibet and China.",
  "description": "Nepali architecture or Nepalese architecture is influenced by the architecture of India, Tibet and China. The pagoda architectural tradition figures prominently among Hindu temples in the country. In contrast, Buddhist temples reflect the Tibetan tradition of Buddhist architecture and the stupa features prominently. Mugal, summit and dome styles also have great scope in Nepal. Whilst significant influence for Nepal's architecture comes from India, there is also a distinct influence from the Newar people.",
